                <pb facs="0195" n="143" xml:id="pg143"/>

                <head>66. Memorandum From the Acting Director of the United States Information
                    Agency (Loomis) to the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Kissinger)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d66-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1970-01-13">January 13, 1970</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>PsyWar Operations Against Vietnamese Communists</item>
                </list>
                <p>As requested in your memorandum of December 15, 1969,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d66-f2"/> to the Secretary of Defense and the Director of the U.S.
                    Information Agency, the attached assessment of programs designed to affect
                    morale of the Communists and Communist sympathizers in Viet-Nam is
                    submitted.</p>
                <p>The assessment was prepared in collaboration with the Commander-in-Chief, Pacific
                    (CINCPAC); the Joint United States Public Affairs Office (JUSPAO), Saigon; and
                    the Military Assistance Command, Viet-Nam (MACV). It was coordinated with the
                    Department of Defense, which is submitting a separate but similar
                        document.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d66-f3"/></p>
                <p>Because he is out of the country, Mr. Shakespeare has not read the
                    assessment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_LH_1">Henry Loomis<anchor n="4" xml:id="d66-f4"/></signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d66-a1.xml" xpointer="d66-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d66-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d66-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 293,
                    Agency Files, USIA—Vol. I [Apr 69–25 Feb 70]. Top Secret. A stamped notation in
                    the top right-hand corner of the memorandum reads: “Staff has action.” Below
                    this, an unknown hand wrote “J. Holdridge.” Another notation in an unknown hand
                    reads: “T.L. (info).”</p>
            </note>
